From: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: core: demote non-default NAPI weight diagnostic

The MediaTek Ethernet driver deliberately uses a NAPI weight of 256.
MediaTek documents that the default weight of 64 can reduce peak software
path throughput by up to approximately 1.2 Gbit/s.

The networking core accepts the larger value, but reports it as an error.
Keep the diagnostic visible while classifying this intentional downstream
tuning as a warning. This does not change the configured weight or any NAPI
data-path behaviour.
---
 net/core/dev.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/core/dev.c
+++ b/net/core/dev.c
@@ -7490,7 +7490,7 @@ void netif_napi_add_weight_locked(struct
 	napi->skb = NULL;
 	napi->poll = poll;
 	if (weight > NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT)
-		netdev_err_once(dev, "%s() called with weight %d\n", __func__,
+		netdev_warn_once(dev, "%s() called with weight %d\n", __func__,
 				weight);
 	napi->weight = weight;
 	napi->dev = dev;
